 A record without `providers`, or a mapping entry without `provider`, predates this
 contract: treat its scope as unknown and re-resolve it from the installed outputs rather
 than assuming every provider was covered.
+
+## Copilot and shared provider outputs
+
+Resolve Copilot destinations and `.agent.md` extensions from the canonical manifest,
+including its MCP path. Harvest
+Copilot agent frontmatter through its renderer mapping; do not promote native tool
+aliases, strict-tools flags, instruction inheritance flags or native model IDs as
+Claude-specific canonical fields. Preserve unsupported local customizations explicitly.
+A shared `.mcp.json` follows the shared-output contract above. When migrating separate
+provider records for the same path, consolidate them only when their recorded baseline
+and observation hashes agree. Preserve conflicting history and use the unknown-history
+migration procedure otherwise; do not choose one provider's baseline silently.
+Never infer its sole owner from a path that multiple providers read. Existing editor
+configuration, server entries and local authentication remain local unless deliberately
+selected for generalization. Changing another installed provider's shared behavior
+requires an explicit resolved scope, even during a single-provider apply.
